  "term": "psychoneuroimmunology",
  "definition": "Psychoneuroimmunology is the study of how the brain, behavior, and the immune system influence one another. It examines how neuropsychological, brain-based, and psychosocial factors can strengthen or weaken immune and allergic responses.",
